<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Additional Method Details</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide a derivation of the gradients for the proposed Distributional Regularization Loss (<math id="S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{DRL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{DRL}</annotation></semantics></math>) under asymmetric temperature settings. We specifically analyze how the temperatures <math id="S6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> interact and modulate the optimization through their gradients.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> be the logits produced by two VLMs. The softened probability distributions <math id="S6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{A,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{A,i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{B,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{B,i}</annotation></semantics></math> are obtained via the softmax function with temperatures <math id="S6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively:</p>
<table id="S6.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{A,i}=\frac{\exp(z_{A,i}/\tau_{A})}{\sum_{j}\exp(z_{A,j}/\tau_{A})},\quad P_{B,i}=\frac{\exp(z_{B,i}/\tau_{B})}{\sum_{j}\exp(z_{B,j}/\tau_{B})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{A,i}=\frac{\exp(z_{A,i}/\tau_{A})}{\sum_{j}\exp(z_{A,j}/\tau_{A})},\quad P_{B,i}=\frac{\exp(z_{B,i}/\tau_{B})}{\sum_{j}\exp(z_{B,j}/\tau_{B})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The Distributional Regularization Loss (DRL) is defined as a weighted Jensen-Shannon divergence (JS), where each Kullback-Leibler (<math id="S6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{KL}</annotation></semantics></math>) term is scaled by the square of its respective temperature to ensure gradient stability:</p>
<table id="S6.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{DRL}=\frac{\tau_{A}^{2}}{2}\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{A}||\mathcal{M})+\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}}{2}\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{B}||\mathcal{M})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{DRL}=\frac{\tau_{A}^{2}}{2}\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{A}||\mathcal{M})+\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}}{2}\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{B}||\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=\frac{1}{2}(P_{A}+P_{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=\frac{1}{2}(P_{A}+P_{B})</annotation></semantics></math> represents the mixed distribution.
The partial derivative with respect to <math id="S6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{A,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{A,i}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="S6.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{DRL}}{\partial z_{A,i}}=\frac{\tau_{A}^{2}}{2}\frac{\partial\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{A}||\mathcal{M})}{\partial z_{A,i}}+\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}}{2}\frac{\partial\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{B}||\mathcal{M})}{\partial z_{A,i}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{DRL}}{\partial z_{A,i}}=\frac{\tau_{A}^{2}}{2}\frac{\partial\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{A}||\mathcal{M})}{\partial z_{A,i}}+\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}}{2}\frac{\partial\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{B}||\mathcal{M})}{\partial z_{A,i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Using the softmax derivative <math id="S6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial P_{A,j}}{\partial z_{A,i}}=\frac{1}{\tau_{A}}P_{A,j}(\delta_{ij}-P_{A,i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial P_{A,j}}{\partial z_{A,i}}=\frac{1}{\tau_{A}}P_{A,j}(\delta_{ij}-P_{A,i})</annotation></semantics></math>, we analyze the two components:</p>
<ul id="S6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Self-term: Expanding the derivative of <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{A}||\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{A}||\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math> yields:</p>
<table id="S6.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\frac{\tau_{A}^{2}}{2}\frac{\partial\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{A}||\mathcal{M})}{\partial z_{A,i}}&amp;=\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}P_{A,i}\left(\log\frac{P_{A,i}}{\mathcal{M}_{i}}-\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{A}||\mathcal{M})\right.\\
&amp;\quad\left.-\frac{P_{A,i}}{2\mathcal{M}_{i}}+\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}\left[\frac{P_{A}}{2\mathcal{M}}\right]\right)\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\frac{\tau_{A}^{2}}{2}\frac{\partial\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{A}||\mathcal{M})}{\partial z_{A,i}}&amp;=\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}P_{A,i}\left(\log\frac{P_{A,i}}{\mathcal{M}_{i}}-\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{A}||\mathcal{M})\right.\\
&amp;\quad\left.-\frac{P_{A,i}}{2\mathcal{M}_{i}}+\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}\left[\frac{P_{A}}{2\mathcal{M}}\right]\right)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes expectation of probability distribution A.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Cross-term: Since <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed relative to <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, the gradient flows only through the mixed distribution <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> in the denominator of the KL term:</p>
<table id="S6.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}}{2}\frac{\partial\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{B}||\mathcal{M})}{\partial z_{A,i}}=-\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}}{2\tau_{A}}P_{A,i}\left(\frac{P_{B,i}}{2\mathcal{M}_{i}}-\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}\left[\frac{P_{B}}{2\mathcal{M}}\right]\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}}{2}\frac{\partial\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{B}||\mathcal{M})}{\partial z_{A,i}}=-\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}}{2\tau_{A}}P_{A,i}\left(\frac{P_{B,i}}{2\mathcal{M}_{i}}-\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}\left[\frac{P_{B}}{2\mathcal{M}}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To simplify the expression, let <math id="S6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}=\frac{P_{B,i}}{P_{A,i}+P_{B,i}}=\frac{P_{B,i}}{2\mathcal{M}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}=\frac{P_{B,i}}{P_{A,i}+P_{B,i}}=\frac{P_{B,i}}{2\mathcal{M}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the relative contribution of Cross-term to the mixture at index <math id="S6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, <math id="S6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{P_{A,i}}{2\mathcal{M}_{i}}=1-V_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{P_{A,i}}{2\mathcal{M}_{i}}=1-V_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting <math id="S6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> into the Self-term:</p>
<table id="S6.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Self-term}=\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}P_{A,i}\left(\log\frac{P_{A,i}}{\mathcal{M}_{i}}-\mathcal{D}_{KL}\right)-\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}P_{A,i}\left((1-V_{i})-\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}[1-V]\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Self-term</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Self-term}=\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}P_{A,i}\left(\log\frac{P_{A,i}}{\mathcal{M}_{i}}-\mathcal{D}_{KL}\right)-\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}P_{A,i}\left((1-V_{i})-\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}[1-V]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Using the linearity of expectation <math id="S6.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}[1-V]=1-\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}[V]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}[1-V]=1-\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}[V]</annotation></semantics></math>, the constant terms cancel out:</p>
<table id="S6.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Self-term}=\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}P_{A,i}\left(\log\frac{P_{A,i}}{\mathcal{M}_{i}}-\mathcal{D}_{KL}\right)+\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}P_{A,i}\left(V_{i}-\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}[V]\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Self-term</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Self-term}=\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}P_{A,i}\left(\log\frac{P_{A,i}}{\mathcal{M}_{i}}-\mathcal{D}_{KL}\right)+\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}P_{A,i}\left(V_{i}-\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}[V]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Combining the adjusted Self-term and the Cross-term:</p>
<table id="S6.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{A,i}}=\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}P_{A,i}\left(\log\frac{P_{A,i}}{\mathcal{M}_{i}}-\mathcal{D}_{KL}\right)+\left(\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}-\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}}{2\tau_{A}}\right)P_{A,i}(V_{i}-\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}[V])" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{A,i}}=\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}P_{A,i}\left(\log\frac{P_{A,i}}{\mathcal{M}_{i}}-\mathcal{D}_{KL}\right)+\left(\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}-\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}}{2\tau_{A}}\right)P_{A,i}(V_{i}-\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}[V])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p4.4" class="ltx_p">The coefficient in the second term can be rewritten as:</p>
<table id="S6.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}-\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}}{2\tau_{A}}=\frac{\tau_{A}^{2}-\tau_{B}^{2}}{2\tau_{A}}=-\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}-\tau_{A}^{2}}{2\tau_{A}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}-\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}}{2\tau_{A}}=\frac{\tau_{A}^{2}-\tau_{B}^{2}}{2\tau_{A}}=-\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}-\tau_{A}^{2}}{2\tau_{A}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p4.5" class="ltx_p">This results in the final simplified form for the gradient with respect to <math id="S6.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{A,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{A,i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S6.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{A,i}}&amp;=\underbrace{\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}P_{A,i}\left(\log\frac{P_{A,i}}{\mathcal{M}_{i}}-\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{A}||\mathcal{M})\right)}_{\textbf{Basic Alignment}}\\
&amp;\quad-\underbrace{\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}-\tau_{A}^{2}}{2\tau_{A}}P_{A,i}\left(\frac{P_{B,i}}{P_{A,i}+P_{B,i}}-\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}\left[\frac{P_{B}}{P_{A}+P_{B}}\right]\right)}_{\textbf{Asymmetric Shift Force}}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Basic Alignment</mtext></munder></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Asymmetric Shift Force</mtext></munder></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial z_{A,i}}&amp;=\underbrace{\frac{\tau_{A}}{2}P_{A,i}\left(\log\frac{P_{A,i}}{\mathcal{M}_{i}}-\mathcal{D}_{KL}(P_{A}||\mathcal{M})\right)}_{\textbf{Basic Alignment}}\\
&amp;\quad-\underbrace{\frac{\tau_{B}^{2}-\tau_{A}^{2}}{2\tau_{A}}P_{A,i}\left(\frac{P_{B,i}}{P_{A,i}+P_{B,i}}-\mathbb{E}_{P_{A}}\left[\frac{P_{B}}{P_{A}+P_{B}}\right]\right)}_{\textbf{Asymmetric Shift Force}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Comparing the results for <math id="S6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{A,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{A,i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{B,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{B,i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we observe an Asymmetric Shift Force modulated by the temperature difference <math id="S6.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\tau^{2}=|\tau_{A}^{2}-\tau_{B}^{2}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\tau^{2}=|\tau_{A}^{2}-\tau_{B}^{2}|</annotation></semantics></math>.
When <math id="S6.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tau_{B}^{2}-\tau_{A}^{2})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tau_{B}^{2}-\tau_{A}^{2})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the DRL formulation (Eq. <a href="#S6.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 6 Additional Method Details ‣ Enhancing Lightweight Vision Language Models through Group Competitive Learning for Socially Compliant Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) degenerates to the standard JS divergence.
When <math id="S6.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tau_{B}^{2}-\tau_{A}^{2})&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tau_{B}^{2}-\tau_{A}^{2})&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the DRL formulation (Eq. <a href="#S6.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 6 Additional Method Details ‣ Enhancing Lightweight Vision Language Models through Group Competitive Learning for Socially Compliant Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) changes to the general distillation loss.
When <math id="S6.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tau_{B}^{2}-\tau_{A}^{2})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tau_{B}^{2}-\tau_{A}^{2})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, smaller models <math id="S6.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, with their limited parameter capacity, are highly susceptible to overfitting and often produce non-smooth output probability distributions. Assigning a high temperature <math id="S6.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{high}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{high}</annotation></semantics></math> to the smaller model explicitly smooths its originally sharp output probabilities. This not only serves as a powerful regularization mechanism but also compels the smaller model to learn soft inter-class relationships. In contrast, larger models <math id="S6.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> possess abundant parameters and strong representational capacity, yet remain prone to overconfidence on training data. Setting a low temperature <math id="S6.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{low}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{low}</annotation></semantics></math> for the larger model enables accurate prediction while introducing mild regularization through the guiding influence of the smaller model’s high temperature outputs, thereby effectively mitigating overconfidence.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Additional Experiment Details</h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section we provide the experimental implementation details and presents supplementary experimental results.</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.1 </span>Additional Implementation Details</h3>

<div id="S7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure a fair comparison, all experiments are conducted on 8 NVIDIA RTX 8000 GPUs, utilizing DeepSpeed ZeRO-3 for distributed training with the Adam optimizer. The learning rate follows a cosine annealing schedule, with all models trained for 10 epochs and a warmup ratio of 0.1.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.2 </span>Additional Main Results Details</h3>

<figure id="S7.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S7.T3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S7.T3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Performance of GCL across 12 competitive group on MUSON.<span id="S7.T3.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="S7.T3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{guide}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{guide}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.T3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{learner}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{learner}</annotation></semantics></math> are allocated to SFT baseline superiority. The performance hierarchy from lowest to highest is: </span>Qwen3-VL-2B (0.805) <math id="S7.T3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math> Qwen2.5-VL-3B (0.811) <math id="S7.T3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math> Qwen2.5-VL-7B (0.829) <math id="S7.T3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math> Qwen3-VL-4B (0.863) <math id="S7.T3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math> Qwen3-VL-8B (0.873).<span id="S7.T3.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Meanwhile, temperature parameters (<math id="S7.T3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.T3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{G}</annotation></semantics></math>) are assigned solely based on parameter size (larger capacity = 2.0, smaller capacity = 3.0). <math id="S7.T3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F1</annotation></semantics></math> denotes Action-F1. Bold text indicates optimal performance of the model.</span></span></figcaption>
<div id="S7.T3.7" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:135.9pt;vertical-align:-66.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-105.3pt,41.5pt) scale(0.620931098401889,0.620931098401889) ;">
<table id="S7.T3.7.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S7.T3.7.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T3.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" colspan="4"><span id="S7.T3.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="S7.T3.7.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S7.T3.7.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S7.T3.7.1.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S7.T3.7.1.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><span id="S7.T3.7.1.1.1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Regime A: Reshaping Mode</span></span></span>
<span id="S7.T3.7.1.1.1.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S7.T3.7.1.1.1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><span id="S7.T3.7.1.1.1.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Capacity<sub id="S7.T3.7.1.1.1.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">L</sub> &lt; Capacity<sub id="S7.T3.7.1.1.1.2.1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_sub">G</sub>,  Small <math id="S7.T3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Large,  <math id="S7.T3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\eta_{learner}=1\times 10^{-5}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" lspace="0.222em" mathvariant="bold" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>𝟏𝟎</mn><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">−</mo><mn>𝟓</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\eta_{learner}=1\times 10^{-5}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S7.T3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\eta_{guide}=5\times 10^{-6}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟓</mn><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" lspace="0.222em" mathvariant="bold" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>𝟏𝟎</mn><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">−</mo><mn>𝟔</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\eta_{guide}=5\times 10^{-6}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span>
</span></span><span id="S7.T3.7.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text"></span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T3.7.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T3.7.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S7.T3.7.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model Group (Learner / Guide)</span></td>
